{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WGE9RpgUgCVEyn2oYkmh7p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's an experiment in specification-driven development using an AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` per utility, `pkg/testutils/` for differential testing, `pkg/sys/` for syscall abstractions, `pkg/format/` for output formatting, `pkg/encutil/` for encoding, `pkg/hashutil/` for checksums. Specs live in `docs/specs/`.\n\n**Current state**: Many utilities across releases 00.0-08.1 are implemented. Several have gaps (not-started items) but their SRD requirements are not in \"ready\" state. The `requirement_states` field shows ready requirements starting from release 09.1 onward.\n\n**Next release**: Release 09.1 (encoding utilities: base32, base64, basenc). base64 (srd080) and basenc (srd081) have all requirements in \"ready\" state. base32 does not appear in requirement_states, so it cannot be proposed.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nEarliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **09.1**. Both srd080-base64 (11 requirements) and srd081-basenc (12 requirements) are fully ready. Both depend on pkg/encutil (srd088, already implemented) and pkg/sys (already implemented).\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0: srd080-base64 R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd080-base64 R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd080-base64 R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd081-basenc R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1), R1.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/base64 encoding mode (srd080-base64 R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd080-base64.yaml (full SRD -- requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - pkg/encutil/ (encoding utility library -- read all .go files for EncoderConfig, Encode, OpenInput exports)\n      - pkg/sys/ (SIGPIPE handler -- read all .go files for InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/base64/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: base64 utility -- encoding mode with flag parsing, wrap control, stdin/file input\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.1 -- parse command-line flags for -w/--wrap column width and --help/--version\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.2 -- encode stdin or file arguments to Base64 and write to stdout\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.3 -- wrap encoded output at column 76 by default, configurable via -w; -w 0 disables wrapping\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd080-base64 R1.4 -- read from stdin when no file arguments are given or when the file argument is '-'\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/encutil.Encode with an EncoderConfig whose Encode field is set to standard Base64 encoding and WrapCol is set from the -w flag (default 76)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/encutil.OpenInput for file/stdin handling\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/base64/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/base64 ./cmd/base64/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"echo 'hello' | go run ./cmd/base64/ produces valid Base64 output\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Default wrap column is 76; -w 0 disables line wrapping\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"File arguments and stdin (no args or '-') both work as input\"\n      - id: AC